    {
      "id": "tt21035364:0:4",
      "title": "Lost in Kowloon",
      "season": 0,
      "episode": 4,
      "number": 4,
      "released": "2001-03-25T00:00:00.000Z",
      "overview": "HAJIME (Ryosuke Yamada), the grandson of the prestigious Kindaichi Detective and his childhood friend, MIYUKI (Haruna Kawaguchi) arrive in Hong Kong so Miyuki can participate in a fashion show as a fill-in for Yang Ran, a model gone missing. While the friends are sightseeing, Miyuki is suddenly abducted. Hajime soon finds out that Yang and Miyuki are exact look alikes and that Yang has a tattoo, signifying the location of the \"Kowloon Treasure\"--rumored to be worth billions of money and guarded by a man known as the \"Kowloon Emperor\". Was Miyuki mistakenly kidnapped instead of Yang? In his search to rescue Miyuki, Hajime is drawn into a string of murders connected to the treasure which has been lost for two decades.... What is the truth behind the mysterious treasure and will Hajime be able to save Miyuki...alive?",
      "thumbnail": "https://episodes.metahub.space/tt21035364/0/4/w780.jpg",
      "moviedb_id": 825795
    },
    {
      "id": "tt21035364:0:5",
      "title": "The Murder Case of Vampire Legend",
      "season": 0,
      "episode": 5,
      "number": 5,
      "released": "2005-09-24T00:00:00.000Z",
      "overview": "When the head of the touring magician’s group \"Magical Fantasy\" is murdered on a train while on his way to Hokkaido, young Kindaichi, who also just happens to be on board, is fast on the case to find the culprit. But just as quickly as the case unfolds, the body disappears only to be rediscovered again, along with other new bodies",
      "thumbnail": "https://episodes.metahub.space/tt21035364/0/5/w780.jpg",
      "moviedb_id": 825793
    },
